::ENG4_U01_L06_GP_Q1::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: Before changing the schedule for a public study center, the planning team gathered feedback from students, tutors, and local employers. The comments did not produce complete consensus, but they revealed a shared concern: evening access mattered for students who worked during the day. What does consensus mean? {
~A. A single recommendation#This is not consensus.
=B. General agreement#Correct. Consensus means general agreement.
~C. A stakeholder group#This names affected people, not agreement.
~D. A trial period#This is a testing period.
}
::ENG4_U01_L06_GP_Q2::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: The team recommended extending hours twice a week and reviewing attendance data after three months. Which paraphrase is accurate? {
=A. The team suggested trying later hours two times each week and checking attendance after three months.#Correct. This preserves the recommendation.
~B. The team permanently changed the schedule every night.#This overstates the recommendation.
~C. The team rejected all schedule changes.#This contradicts the passage.
~D. The team studied attendance before making any recommendation.#The passage says attendance would be reviewed after three months.
}
::ENG4_U01_L06_GP_Q3::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: This recommendation was credible because it responded to stakeholder concerns, used a limited trial period, and included a plan for evaluating results. Which word best describes people affected by a decision? {
~A. Consensus#Consensus is agreement.
~B. Rationale#Rationale is reasoning.
=C. Stakeholders#Correct. Stakeholders are affected people or groups.
~D. Recommendation#A recommendation is suggested action.
}
::ENG4_U01_L06_GP_Q4::[MLA.ENG4.C.01] Passage: This recommendation was credible because it responded to stakeholder concerns, used a limited trial period, and included a plan for evaluating results. Which oral explanation is most coherent? {
~A. The plan was good and had people and data and it worked.#This is vague.
~B. The recommendation is consensus because it is credible because students exist.#This misuses terms.
~C. The plan is about evening access, so it is definitely perfect.#This overstates the passage.
=D. The recommendation is credible because it addresses stakeholder concerns, tests the change for a limited time, and reviews attendance data.#Correct. This is organized and precise.
}
::ENG4_U01_L06_GP_Q5::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: This recommendation was credible because it responded to stakeholder concerns, used a limited trial period, and included a plan for evaluating results. Which word best means the reason for a choice? {
~A. Stakeholder#A stakeholder is an affected person or group.
=B. Rationale#Correct. A rationale explains the reason behind a choice.
~C. Consensus#Consensus means agreement.
~D. Schedule#A schedule is a time plan.
}
